      "side": 1,
      "message": "Print the whole failed command line:\n\n  error \"dut-control command failed: $(${DUT_CONTROL_CMD[*]} $*)\"\n\nConsider putting the whole command line into an ARGS variable before executing/erroring, e.g:\n\n  local ARGS\u003d( \"${DUT_CONTROL_CMD[@]}\" \"$@\" )\n\nThen down here you can do:\n\n  error \"dut-control command failed: ${ARGS[*]}\"\n\nNote use of * instead of @ in the error line (but not when actually running dut-control!).",
